## Databricks Marketplace v1 packaging, ported to 0.10.0

Context: The Marketplace v1 (built and tested on the 0.7 base, 2026-11-03,
.planning/marketplace-listing/PLAN.md) is redone on top of the 0.10.0 branch.
0.10.0 removed the UC Volume (8fad03ff), moved the Help Center to docs/, split
SettingsService, and adds a `sql` user scope.

Already fixed upstream in 0.10.0:
- the token write in /settings/save;
- the assistant route using caller credentials.

Ported here:
- the session-host rejection;
- the /api/v1 credential hardening.

Findings while porting:
- The SDK's AppManifest model has no Postgres/Lakebase resource spec, so
  Lakebase becomes a post-install binding (Q1).
- A Marketplace install has no source for REGISTRY_CATALOG / REGISTRY_SCHEMA
  (new Q7).
- 0.10.0 failed to start under `uv run --no-dev`, because httpx is imported at
  runtime but was a dev-only dependency. Fixed here.

Changes:

1. marketplace/app.yaml, marketplace/manifest.yaml (new on this branch)
   Fixed config for 0.10.x. The manifest declares the SQL warehouse only, plus
   user_api_scopes [sql]. app.yaml ships the warehouse valueFrom and Settings
   defaults, and mirrors the template's authorization block. No Volume, no
   Postgres spec.
2. marketplace/LISTING.md, marketplace/README.md (new on this branch)
   New post-install steps: bind Lakebase, grant the service principal Can
   Manage on the app, then Initialize. Adds the 0.10.x port notes and the
   test-install runbook.
3. scripts/marketplace/assemble.py (new on this branch)
   Ships src/ (minus mcp-server and .coding_rules.md) and the Help Center set
   docs/*.md + docs/images/ + docs/screenshots/, mirroring databricks.yml sync
   and .databricksignore. The bundle is 15 MB (was 28 MB).
4. scripts/marketplace/emulate_install.py (new on this branch)
   No Volume. Grants the manifest's user_api_scopes, using update mask
   resources,user_api_scopes on re-runs. Lakebase is bound as the post-install
   step.
5. Makefile
   marketplace-bundle and marketplace-test-install targets (run via
   uv run --frozen).
6. src/back/objects/domain/settings/WarehouseSettings.py
   apply_config_save rejects a caller host in Apps mode before writing it.
7. src/api/routers/v1.py
   get_credentials uses only the app service principal in Apps mode. OpenAPI
   descriptions no longer ask for a PAT.
8. pyproject.toml, uv.lock
   httpx moved to the runtime dependencies. The lock edit is two lines in the
   ontobricks package block; no download URLs changed. Re-run
   `uv lock --no-config --default-index https://pypi.org/simple` where there is
   network, to regenerate the lock.
9. tests/units/scripts/test_marketplace_package.py, test_marketplace_assemble.py, test_marketplace_emulate_install.py (new on this branch)
   - Drift guards against the 0.10.0 template.
   - The authorization block and manifest scopes match the template.
   - The manifest stays inside the SDK's AppManifest model.
   - The Help Center payload is right.
   - Install plan: scopes, no Volume, Lakebase as the post-install binding.
10. tests/units/settings/test_no_pat_in_app_mode.py, tests/units/api/test_v1_credentials.py, tests/units/api/test_assistant_invoke_credentials.py (new on this branch)
    - Host rejection.
    - The upstream "token never stored" behaviour.
    - /api/v1 credentials.
    - The assistant always overwrites caller credentials (regression guard for
      the upstream fix).
11. .planning/marketplace-listing/PLAN.md
    Q7 added, plus the Q1 evidence and the 0.10.0 status.

