Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" --deselect tests/units/api/test_routes.py::TestHealthRoutes --deselect tests/units/core/test_health.py::TestRunReadinessChecks → 10336 passed, 324 skipped, 13 deselected in 65.8s.
The deselected health/readiness tests make live network calls (urllib3 retry backoff against test.databricks.com), which hang in the sandbox this ran in. CI with network runs them as usual.

## Marketplace v1 on 0.10.0: E2 dogfood test install

Context: The 0.10.0 bundle was installed into E2 dogfood as
ontobricks-mp-test-010, the Marketplace way: warehouse and the `sql` scope at
install, the Lakebase project ontobricks-mp-test-010 bound as the post-install
step, no bootstrap scripts.

Results:
- The app starts (so the httpx fix works).
- Q4 reproduces: everyone is locked out until the service principal gets
  CAN_MANAGE on the app.
- Q7 is confirmed: Initialize returns 400 without REGISTRY_CATALOG /
  REGISTRY_SCHEMA. With them supplied as a test-only deployment env_vars
  override, Initialize succeeds and readiness shows 0 errors.
- The Lakebase project lookup (walking every project to match PGHOST) aborts in
  large workspaces, so the registry location saved in Lakebase is never read
  back after a redeploy.
- Credential checks: host returns 400, token isn't stored, /api/v1 runs as the
  service principal.

Changes:

1. marketplace/README.md
   0.10.0 results section.
2. .planning/marketplace-listing/PLAN.md
   0.10.0 live-test status, including the Lakebase project-walk finding.

Modified files:
- marketplace/README.md
- .planning/marketplace-listing/PLAN.md

Tests: docs only. Live checks on https://ontobricks-mp-test-010-6051921418418893.staging.aws.databricksapps.com:
- app RUNNING
- Initialize: 400 without the registry vars, 200 with them
- readiness: 0 errors after Initialize
- /settings/save host: 400
- /api/v1 with a bogus token: 200, runs as the service principal
